  "excitation_report": "New term = meiotic-drive distortion -s_meiotic*p*(1-p)*p/(k_md+p) (child minus parent). With sigma=0.0006 on the p-trajectory it reaches a peak deviation of 0.00510 = 8.51*sigma, strongest early at t~2.7 gen (where p is still near its max 0.05 and the ~p^2 meiotic term is largest before the allele declines). Comfortably above the 5*sigma bar. The four ancestral terms (mean-fitness directional selection, frequency-dependent selection toward p_star, inbreeding-depression loss, and finite-N_e drift bias) were excited in prior evolution steps and remain O(1e-2) contributors to dp_dt, far above sigma; only the new mechanism was gated here.",
